[{"id":"VRCE-7-53-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":1,"english":"When the sages had spoken thus, Käkutstha said: \"O ascetics, tell me what is the work which I shall have to accomplish in your behalf. Your fear shall be removed.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.614,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"504d98075a3195c067f64973c7aa6a9dcaa2fed0be2ea18f4068439616dec56a","compact":"0a07190ebbf1e7853a46827bd3eedc6254bf1f1e652b9225f42e78c147c1c921","nasal":"0a07190ebbf1e7853a46827bd3eedc6254bf1f1e652b9225f42e78c147c1c921"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":2,"english":"As Käkutstha was speaking thus, Bhārgava remarked! O lord of men, do you hear of the origin of the fear that threatens our country.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5421b60b2a402d1c2786e028e29087f3475213ccb53d92c3f5cdd51bd4377da","compact":"dcd3cd6346b986759928c2967f8c0588b4e0aa934be1e871e836d1c4c171ddde","nasal":"dcd3cd6346b986759928c2967f8c0588b4e0aa934be1e871e836d1c4c171ddde"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":3,"english":"O king, formerly in the Kita age, there was a magnanimous offspring of Diti, the mighty Asura, Madhu, eldest son of Lotā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.617,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0480a58b537700362f07c0f3aca6b1cf3821e4ac08aabaf0906009e3fd154de0","compact":"5ef1792df6e4d5ec9615e3828eda0a4e0364ee0506c637bab1e0dde4ea154a79","nasal":"5ef1792df6e4d5ec9615e3828eda0a4e0364ee0506c637bab1e0dde4ea154a79"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":4,"english":"He was well disposed towards Brāhmaṇas, kind to those seeking his refuge, and gifted with high intelligence. The exceedingly generous deities delighted in him greatly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"46087db8b7babb5bebcca594ff90ab07fe8713cb845f9b859e7a0093283d6c02","compact":"1295a25d5b298c758ee9ed010563fab81a12f3c8b59043ef5018b042b0002340","nasal":"1295a25d5b298c758ee9ed010563fab81a12f3c8b59043ef5018b042b0002340"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":5,"english":"And by way of honouring him, Rudra conferred a wonderful boon upon Madhu endowed with prowess and ever intent on religion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0ad0605c198032076fc971eed6169d57ebc8b604ed9096b574995a44b81631c","compact":"20657bf8e5bb8cb1226e9cdbac2becda3ccc2756eb95c7156504fb0fa83f72fd","nasal":"9311f77bfe1ff9b7ef263f41f1daafeb046cbe29c328f2b24d0efaf8a04b71f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":6,"english":"And extracting a dart from his own, possessed of terrific energy, endowed with great force; and furnished with exceeding splendour that highsouled one, well pleased, made it over (to Madhu) and spoke to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbad0cad255450dbec86131e66096694284923b11c30af42d0828a69ced67170","compact":"40837ffe1801a9f146cab5b5762e8523a5b9acf051baa504fd17cca12fac0ccf","nasal":"40837ffe1801a9f146cab5b5762e8523a5b9acf051baa504fd17cca12fac0ccf"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":7,"english":"You have practised excellent and unrivalled righteousness, which has won my good graces, and (therefore), I highly gratified, bestow on you this choice weapon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81a9e4fee03568177b356df6cfc683df20a3dbea784f5a2df0cea2f0654504f3","compact":"fc9cb02b1ce84becbf6014d64597977319112bc24ec71e13a4cbb223fd22bcfb","nasal":"fc9cb02b1ce84becbf6014d64597977319112bc24ec71e13a4cbb223fd22bcfb"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":8,"english":"So long as you, O mighty Asura, do not assail celestials and Vipras, so long shall this be your, otherwise it shall come to naught.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f1f140b1ac30a1c21b8b124b6ab42e8d6d90090e40f88fd125113d75bbd2fd5","compact":"4207b64b7ad98fe3c7b3fd00a4825532b9d97c8c42b2f119d5a000e1eb5774be","nasal":"4207b64b7ad98fe3c7b3fd00a4825532b9d97c8c42b2f119d5a000e1eb5774be"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":9,"english":"Reducing to cinders the person that shall rashly enter upon conflict with you, this dart shall return to your hand.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.762,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d247079f3922933ff1dfa8dafead69faaa6d3eb32aad9bb71b5bba6fa1cdbea7","compact":"a7978d9cb0609c6c9b9b671d9651d396ce58715354befe9265d420bab8305da2","nasal":"88e7848ddeb248e3409d4a5d18694e0ca0bf7f80688c325df2d6d212afefab0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":10,"english":"Having thus obtained the boon from Rudra, the mighty Asura, again bowing to Mahādeva, addressed him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5afe6bd4e0d5bafbae6ad06ae025f12f423e68fafedf4884760a59a3644bd4e0","compact":"86d9a87ca4da81f1a3bf8b5980dd0008356fb36207222533798411fd142001a6","nasal":"86d9a87ca4da81f1a3bf8b5980dd0008356fb36207222533798411fd142001a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":11,"english":"O reverend one, may this excellent dart be the possession of my family O god, you are the lord of the immortals.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43ab97cb4180901548ecab38e304df661cbd0acc900fce87fad72a1f6000dd96","compact":"41ec81314b2e704b962f8c54987abeaca88368aac772eb28a56628429d03af92","nasal":"de9bf0bcce1e997729b55867264d393d8836356f9e75674e35e802275c490349"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":12,"english":"Thereat the lord of all beings, the mighty deity Śiva, answered Madhu, when he had spoken thus: This will not be.","alig