 a splendid city to be constructed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"465efb73efcb0544e2e361c33b854bc0a75427d46f148d8cdfb20d60adc71a09","compact":"dccd814fc71ebbb2cd2318468a5afe17c750e76d95d223173187d3e9e7e5eac6","nasal":"6cfb8fba3357fd6854c7bb74bdb4d30de6a57dcb2ba76712050a3546c38eb50a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":16,"english":"His beloved wife the exalted and majestic Kumbhīnasſ is the offspring of Viśvāvasu by Anala.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"493fbde58a34f0c00a1d52da7db997a4be2e13c017aee11434bd4605aaf27cb6","compact":"ff4e86a593715eea38ff28849adc5242173991b3b9f3fd7148754cecd59d1a2f","nasal":"7cba2657fe81493d5c77a45e3dafc7decf995b2dfe91e0a46b2fa9da2788d248"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":17,"english":"Her son, the highly powerful wicked, and fierce Lavana, ever since his boyhood, gave himself up to a sinful course of life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c42940349e3aab5b6d0654fda52b826acc4b8ae49eb3d11ce2af8944db4ebf0","compact":"adc702fdb8d5dc5bfb5100589882a9533505363c37bde6799774816eb457f350","nasal":"adc702fdb8d5dc5bfb5100589882a9533505363c37bde6799774816eb457f350"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":18,"english":"Seeing his son, committed to an impious course Madhu was overcome with grief, but he did not say anything to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2431e418ea913a8f348865b75391dd43cf586da46be253df2cb938645b4677af","compact":"404385ac6fecc6369efb0794ae2afb36c8281c3ab7034ad7d89e93dcb65fb68e","nasal":"404385ac6fecc6369efb0794ae2afb36c8281c3ab7034ad7d89e93dcb65fb68e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":19,"english":"And forsaking this world, he entered the region of Varuņa; and making over the dart to Lavana, communicated to him all about the boon he had obtained.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f4657b37fc93b29fdbd1ec78a595fb6940f203f393e75310f525ed593814650","compact":"8dc16ebac387dc0466bd3ba3bd5a673bf30f3d21d6a84175189a039af3e2a002","nasal":"8dc16ebac387dc0466bd3ba3bd5a673bf30f3d21d6a84175189a039af3e2a002"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-53-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":53,"verse":20,"english":"And by virtue of the power of the dart, he oppress the three worlds in especial the ascetics; such is the power of Lavaņa, and such is his dart. Hearing all this O Kākutstha, you are capable (of righting our wrong.) You are our chief resource.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-61-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7053020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"948d1e7855ce0dc9df6351b1e6d1ed05b80161314db7e64e76ea56d5fc0a887d","compact":"ed426952673ee84128608c9894754bfab89ae3